# Scott2026 module layout

## Definitions (MATLAB-style)

- **One `def` / `abbrev` / `noncomputable def` per file**, named after the definition (`rank.lean` → `def rank`).
- Mutual defs (e.g. `memB` / `eqB`) share **one** file when they must be declared together.
- `inductive`, `structure`, and `class` stay in self-named files (already done for structures).
- Each def file: copyright header, **all `import`s first** (Lean requires imports at file top), then `namespace` … single def … `end`.

## Theorems

- **Group lemmas/theorems by topic** in descriptively named files (e.g. `MembershipLaws.lean`, `Fullness.lean`), not one theorem per file.
- Keep topic files **well under 1000 lines**; split by subtopic if a bundle grows large.

## Top level is the paper

`Scott2026/` has two entry files (`Basic.lean`, `Paper.lean`) and four section directories, matching the mathematical sections of the LIPIcs paper. Introduction and Conclusions are not modules. Do not add new siblings at `Scott2026/*.lean`.

| Directory | Paper |
| --- | --- |
| `BooleanValuedSetTheory/` | §2 Boolean-valued set theory |
| `Setoids/` | §3 Boolean-valued setoids |
| `LambdaModels/DomainTheory/` | §4.1 Domain theory and internal interpretation |
| `LambdaModels/Engeler/` | §4.2 The Engeler model |
| `LambdaModels/Oracles/` | §4.3 Injective spaces and oracles |
| `RandomVariables/` | §5 Random variables |

## Large modules → topic subfolders

Inside a section, keep a thin hub plus topic folders. Example: `Scott2026/BooleanValuedSetTheory/VA/AName/rank.lean` → module `Scott2026.BooleanValuedSetTheory.VA.AName.rank`.

- The hub (`VA.lean`, `Random.lean`, …) is a module doc and an import list, not a pile of definitions.

### VA topic map (target)

| Subfolder | Contents |
|-----------|----------|
| `BooleanValuedSetTheory/VA/AName/` | `AName` inductive, `idx`, `child`, `val`, `rank`, `meas`, `memB`/`eqB`, `mix`, `check`, `subsetB`, `nameSetoid`, `homB`, … |
| `BooleanValuedSetTheory/VA/D0Formula/` | `consPSet`, `realize`, `consName`, Δ₀ invariance lemmas |
| `BooleanValuedSetTheory/VA/PSet/` | `pOpair`, `pfinEnum`, `pfin`, … |
| `BooleanValuedSetTheory/VA/SetFormula/` | `rename`, `lift`, `inst`, connectives |
| `BooleanValuedSetTheory/VA/Axioms/` | `extensionalityAxiom`, pairing, union, power, infinity, separation, collection, choice, … |
| `BooleanValuedSetTheory/VA/AName/*.lean` (theorem bundles) | e.g. substitution laws, fullness, mixing — **no new defs** unless extracted from a def file |

Apply the same pattern under the section directories: `RandomVariables/Random/` (`AssociatedAlgebra`, `MeasureAlgebra`, `L0`, …), `RandomVariables/Coin/`, `LambdaModels/DomainTheory/Lambda/`, `LambdaModels/DomainTheory/InternalEval/`.

## Size budget

- **Hard target:** no file over **1000 lines**.
- **Soft target:** most files **200–600 lines**; hubs and small def files often **&lt; 80 lines**.
- When splitting, run `lake build` after each hub or namespace batch; keep the import graph acyclic.

## Imports

- Never place `universe`, `open`, `attribute`, or `namespace` before `import` lines.
- Child modules import only what the def needs; hubs import all siblings in dependency order.
